## Checkbox format (`.cursor/rules/` only)

In **`.cursor/rules/**`** files, **never** use Markdown `- [ ]` / `- [x]`. Use emoji only:

| State | Emoji | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Unchecked · todo gate | ⬜ | `- ⬜ contract brief written` |
| Done · met · pass | ✅ | `- ✅ gates green` |
| Forbidden · must not | ❌ | `- ❌ multi-purpose PR` |

Applies when authoring or editing any rule under `.cursor/rules/`.

---

## Forbidden Shortcuts (absolutely forbidden)

- ❌ Making green by deleting/weakening tests only
- ❌ Production edits before contract brief / failing test (when behavior changes)
- ❌ Multi-purpose PRs (redesign + unrelated cleanup + UI in one diff)
- ❌ Using replay · artifact · metrics as solver · algorithm **inputs**
- ❌ Multiple `route_domain` patches (`RouteDomainSnapshotBuilder` is sole owner)
- ❌ Repair logic in validation (read-only asserts only)
- ❌ Using candidate order as commit order; using candidate reachable as final commit proof
- ❌ Raw↔server re-conversion inside optimization
- ❌ **Free-form strings** for `failure_reason` · `event_type` · `issue_code`, etc. (update enum/const + tests together)
- ❌ Proceeding with implementation before contract/spec exists for contract changes
- ❌ Declaring completion without validation
- ❌ Renames changing **only a leading underscore** (`func`↔`_func`, `name`↔`_name`, same import alias) — style · lint · “private/public cleanup”. **Exception**: user explicitly requests rename, or approved contract · spec requires new name
- ❌ Using superseded or deleted docs as implementation authority
- ❌ Markdown `- [ ]` / `- [x]` in `.cursor/rules/**` — use ⬜ ✅ ❌ per [Checkbox format](#checkbox-format-cursorrules-only) above

Full list: [`testing.md § Forbidden shortcuts`](mdc:documents/ai/manuals/testing.md)

